  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Aircraft Manufacturing (NAICS 336411) federal contracting totaled $44.6B in FY2026 to date. The industry recorded 5,624 awards and an average award size of $7.9M. Obligations are down 27.2% year over year. The Department of Defense accounted for the vast majority of spending and obligated $43.9B. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION and THE BOEING COMPANY were the top suppliers by dollar value, with LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION receiving $11.9B and THE BOEING COMPANY receiving multiple awards totaling $9B, $4.3B, $2.4B, $2B, and $1.8B across separate listings. Other notable vendors included SIKORSKY AIRCRAFT CORPORATION with $2.5B, BELL TEXTRON INC with $1.8B, SIERRA NEVADA COMPANY, LLC with $1.5B, and GENERAL ATOMICS AERONAUTICAL SYSTEMS, INC. with $823M. Past fiscal years show variability, with obligations of $40.7B in FY21, $37.2B in FY22, $60.1B in FY23, $44.2B in FY24, and $61.2B in FY25.",
